# .dockerignore for the mandrel-command workspace-root build context.
#
# Both command images (backend + frontend) build from this directory as context
# (docker-compose.yml: context: ./mandrel-command). Keep the context TIGHT: the
# Dockerfiles COPY manifests + the relevant member source explicitly, so everything
# heavy or irrelevant should be excluded to keep the build fast and the daemon
# transfer small. node_modules in particular is ~1GB+ and must never be sent.

# Dependencies — always reinstalled deterministically from the root lockfile.
node_modules
*/node_modules
**/node_modules
.npm
.pnpm-debug.log*
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Build outputs — regenerated inside the image.
*/dist
*/build
**/dist
**/build

# Logs / runtime data
logs/
*/logs/
*.log
pids/
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
*/uploads/

# Tests & coverage (not needed to build the runtime artifact)
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
coverage/
*/coverage/
.nyc_output
.jest-cache

# Git / VCS
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db

# Docs & misc (markdown, demos, helper scripts) — not part of the build.
*.md
!frontend/src/**/*.md
!backend/src/**/*.md
demo-*.js
demo-*.md
create-admin.js
*/cookies.txt
docs/
*/docs/

# Environment files — secrets must never enter the image (.env.example is allowlisted
# below because dotenv-safe validates against it at runtime).
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.test
.env.production
*/.env
*/.env.local
*/.env.development
*/.env.test
*/.env.production
# `*.local` — THE PER-MACHINE OVERRIDES. This was the hole (measured 2026-07-30):
# every `.env.<mode>` variant above was excluded but NONE of the `.local` ones were,
# and `mandrel-command/frontend/.env.production.local` exists untracked on the build
# host. It is gitignored, so it never shows in a diff or a `git status`; the build
# context is THIS directory, so `COPY frontend/ ./frontend/` pulled it into the image;
# and Vite loads `.env.production.local` at the HIGHEST precedence during
# `npm run build`, above `.env.production` and above the shell environment. The file
# on disk today is inert only by luck — it sets VITE_MCP_BASE_URL while the code reads
# VITE_MCP_URL — so ONE rename would have baked our prod hostname into every tenant's
# bundle with nothing to see in review.
#
# `**` as well as the two literal levels: a .dockerignore pattern matches path
# segments, so a bare `*.local` covers only the context root and `*/.env*.local` only
# one level down. The frontend's own .dockerignore already carried `*.local` — but it
# is NEVER CONSULTED, because Docker reads only the .dockerignore at the CONTEXT root,
# which is this file. Same class as the whole workstream: the rule was written, in the
# wrong place, and looked done.
#
# ⚠️ THIS RULE HAS NOT BEEN PROVEN BY A REAL BUILD. It rests on documented
# .dockerignore semantics and on file inspection, NOT on an observed image. The control host
# control box where this branch was written has no docker (`which docker` -> nothing),
# so no build could be run. Stated here rather than glossed, because an unverified fix
# that READS as verified is the failure mode.
#
# TO CLOSE THE LOOP, on any host that has docker AND the untracked file present
# (it exists today at mandrel-command/frontend/.env.production.local on the mandrel
# dev tree). From the REPO ROOT:
#
#   # 0. precondition — the hazard must actually be present, or the test proves nothing
#   test -f mandrel-command/frontend/.env.production.local || echo "NO HAZARD PRESENT"
#
#   # 1. build the frontend image from the same context compose uses
#   docker build -f mandrel-command/frontend/Dockerfile -t dockerignore-probe \
#       --target builder mandrel-command
#
#   # 2. THE ASSERTION: the file must NOT be in the build stage's context copy.
#   #    Expect NO output. Any line printed = the exclusion FAILED.
#   docker run --rm dockerignore-probe \
#       sh -c 'ls -la /app/frontend/.env.production.local 2>/dev/null'
#
#   # 3. MUTATION CONTROL — prove step 2 can fail. Comment out the three *.local lines
#   #    below, rebuild, re-run step 2: it MUST print the file. Then restore them.
#   #    Without this control a green step 2 could just mean the probe never looked.
#
#   # 4. cleanup
#   docker image rm dockerignore-probe
#
.env*.local
*/.env*.local
**/*.local
!.env.example
!*/.env.example

# Docker / compose files (no need to ship build configs into the image)
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
Dockerfile*

# OpenAPI generated dev files
.openapi/
*/.openapi/

# Temp
tmp/
temp/
*.tgz
*.backup
backups/
